  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 343 PM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nWeak shortwave trough moving through zonal flow aloft will bring\nmedium chance for rain Friday, mainly near the SD border/tri-\nstate area into west-central MN. There is also a low chance for\nshowers in northeast ND into far northern Red River Valley\nFriday. More details on amounts can be found below.\n\nThereafter into the weekend and next week, upper flow becomes \nrelatively week amid upper ridging into central Canada. Ensemble\nguidance also suggests a weak, disorganized shortwave upper \ntrough gradually sliding west to east out of the Northern \nRockies through the Central Plains into mid-Mississippi Valley. \nThis present a weak Rex-block-type pattern late weekend into \nearly/mid next week. This trend in guidance has decreased rain \nchances for our area this weekend, ultimately offering a now \nmostly dry weekend forecast. This will also keep temperatures \nnear average through at least mid next week.\n\nInto mid/late next week, guidance suggests either continued\nweak upper ridging or zonal flow aloft. Both scenarios suggest\ntemperatures trending near average to slightly above average;\nthe former would favor mostly dry conditions, with the later\nscenario bringing at least a slight uptick in rain chances with\nthe possibility of progressive shortwave troughs moving through\nthe region out of the Pacific Northwest.\n\n...Rain chances Friday...\n\nGuidance continues to keep the lion's share of soaking rainfall\nsouth of our area Friday. There is still a subset of guidance \nthat eeks the northern fringes of moderate to briefly heavy \nrainfall into locations near the SD border/tri-state area into\nwest-central MN. Should this occur, rainfall totals may reach\ninto the 0.8-1.5 inch range. There is around a 30% chance for\nthis to occur. Otherwise, most likely amounts are expected to \nremain less than 0.5 inches. The chance for 3 or more inches \nremains very low/nill at this time.\n\nTiming for rainfall in southeast ND into west-central MN begins\nFriday morning around sunrise, lingering through early to mid\nafternoon.\n\nA separate area of showers are expected to develop in portions\nof north-central ND into SK/MB Friday. This could spread into\nnortheast ND and the far northern Red River Valley. Rain amounts\nwill be light, only up to a few hundredths, if this occurs.",
